    "title": "Stanford Defeats No. 14 North Carolina",
    "text": "• Stanford defeated No. 14 North Carolina 95-90 on Wednesday night.\n• The game took place in Stanford, California.\n• Freshman Ebuka Okorie scored 36 points and had nine assists for Stanford.\n• Stanford rallied from a 12-point deficit in the second half.\n• Jeremy Dent-Smith made a go-ahead 3-pointer with 1:04 remaining.\n• Ryan Agarwal hit a 3-pointer to put Stanford up by four points with 32 seconds left.\n• Stanford's record is now 14-4 overall and 3-2 in the ACC.\n• North Carolina's record is now 14-3 overall and 2-2 in the ACC.\n• This is Stanford's second win over a ranked opponent this month.\n• Jeremy Dent-Smith and Ryan Agarwal each scored 20 points for Stanford.\n• Chisom Okpara, Stanford's second-leading scorer, was out with a lower-body injury.\n• Caleb Wilson and Henri Veesaar each scored 26 points for North Carolina.\n• North Carolina will visit California on Saturday.\n• Stanford will host Duke on Saturday.",
